<BaseLayout title="Engine and drivetrain identification">
  <h1>Engine and drivetrain identification</h1>
  <p>The reference vehicle is a 2021 S60 T5 Inscription. T5 is a sales designation; it is not a complete engine or transmission identification.</p>

  <h2>Known vehicle description</h2>
  <table><tbody>
    <tr><th>Model year</th><td>2021</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Model</th><td>Volvo S60</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Trim / powertrain badge</th><td>Inscription / T5</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Engine family</th><td>2.0-liter turbocharged four-cylinder Drive-E gasoline engine</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Drivetrain</th><td>Not yet confirmed — record FWD or AWD from the vehicle/build record</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Transmission code</th><td>Not yet confirmed — verify from VIN-specific service information</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>

  <h2>What to verify before ordering parts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Engine code and production date.</li>
    <li>FWD or AWD configuration.</li>
    <li>Transmission model/code and software version.</li>
    <li>Brake package and rotor dimensions.</li>
    <li>Factory wheel and tire package.</li>
    <li>Installed option codes and market specification.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Identification sources</h2>
  <p>Use the VIN with an authorized Volvo parts/service source or a reliable VIN-specific build record. The VIN is private information: keep the full number out of this public site and GitHub issues. If sharing documentation publicly, redact the VIN and personal details.</p>
</BaseLayout>
